   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "A statement by Yari’s Media Office, said the visits were aimed at strengthening engagement with traditional institutions, foster mutual understanding and seek the support, blessings and counsel of revered traditional leaders as part of the Council’s ongoing nationwide consultations. In his remarks at the Emir of Ilorin’s Palace, Senator Yari expressed confidence in the capacity of the APC to win the presidential, governorship and National and State assemblies seats in the North Central state.",
   "summary_zh": "亚里媒体办公室发表的一份声明称，这些访问旨在加强与传统机构的接触，促进相互理解，并寻求受人尊敬的传统领袖的支持、祝福和建议，作为委员会正在进行的全国协商的一部分。在伊洛林埃米尔宫的讲话中，参议员亚里对APC在北中部州赢得总统职位、州长职位以及国家和州议会席位的能力表示信心。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "A statement by Yari’s Media Office, said the visits were aimed at strengthening engagement with traditional institutions, foster mutual understanding and seek the support, blessings and counsel of revered traditional leaders as part of the Council’s ongoing nationwide consultations. In his remarks at the Emir of Ilorin’s Palace, Senator Yari expressed confidence in the capacity of the APC to win the presidential, governorship and National and State assemblies seats in the North Central state. He cited progress recorded since 2019, including the resolution of past challenges in education and healthcare delivery, the establishment of new hospitals, and far-reaching reforms. Yari reaffirmed that the campaign would leverage on the strength of the party, the landmark achievements of Governor AbdulRahman AbdulRazaq, alongside the Governor’s role as Chairman of the Nigeria Governors’ Forum, to extend its influence nationally. It further noted that the consultative visits underscore its recognition of the pivotal role traditional rulers play in promoting peace, unity, and stability across the country, and reaffirmed its commitment to carrying all stakeholders along in the build-up to the elections. Yari was accompanied on the visits by National Secretary of the party, Senator Ajibola Bashiru; former Kano State Governor, Dr. Abdullahi Umar Ganduje; former Speaker of the House of Representatives, Honourable Aminu Bello Masari. Also on the delegation were Senators Adamu Aliero, Ali Modu Sheriff, Rochas Okorocha, Ahmad Sani Yarima, Mohammed Badaru Abubakar and Danjuma Goje, former governors of Kebbi, Borno, Imo, Zamfara, Jigawa and Gombe states, respectively. Others were Ibrahim Shema, Olusegun Mimiko, former governors of Katsina and Ondo states and Honourable Hon. Dimeji Bankole, former Speaker of the House of Representatives. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel BREAKING NEWS: Nigerians can invest ₦2.5million on premium domains and earn about ₦17-25Million. Earnings in USD. Rather than wonder, click here to find out how it works --> --> James Kwen James Kwen is a journalist with Leadership Media Group with 15 years of experience, currently covering politics, including the National Assembly (House of Representatives), APC, INEC, and allied beats",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
