   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "The All Progressives Congress (APC) Presidential Campaign Council (PCC), has scheduled its inaugural meeting on Tuesday at the Presidential Campaign Council HQ Plot 781, Herbert Macaulay Way, Central Business District, Abuja. According to the notice, the meeting is strictly by invitation to the list of attendees which are the leadership and members of the campaign council.",
   "summary_zh": "全体进步大会党（APC）总统竞选委员会（PCC）已将其首次会议安排在周二于总统竞选委员会总部举行，该总部位于阿布贾中央商务区赫伯特·麦考利路781号地块。根据通知，此次会议严格凭邀请参加，参会者为竞选委员会的领导层和成员。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The All Progressives Congress (APC) Presidential Campaign Council (PCC), has scheduled its inaugural meeting on Tuesday at the Presidential Campaign Council HQ Plot 781, Herbert Macaulay Way, Central Business District, Abuja. This is contained in a notice issued by the Secretary of the Council and govenror of Imo state, Senator Hope Uzodimma on Sunday night. According to the notice, the meeting is strictly by invitation to the list of attendees which are the leadership and members of the campaign council. “You are hereby invited to the inaugural meeting of the APC Presidential Campaign Council, scheduled to hold as follows: Date: Tuesday, 20th, October 2026 Time: 2 PM Prompt Venue: PRESIDENTIAL CAMPAIGN COUNCIL HQ Plot 781, Herbert Macaulay Way, Central Business District (Central Area), Abuja. Attendance: Directors and Secretaries of Directorates “Kindly note that the meeting is strictly by invitation and is open only to the 134 members of the Presidential Campaign Council listed below. “The meeting will formally commence the collective assignment of the Council and provide an opportunity to consider and adopt the Campaign Calendar, as well as to deliberate on other ancillary matters, including preparations for the flag-off of the campaign scheduled to hold in Kaduna on Saturday, 24th October 2026,” the notice read. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel BREAKING NEWS: Nigerians can invest ₦2.5million on premium domains and earn about ₦17-25Million. Earnings in USD. Rather than wonder, click here to find out how it works --> --> James Kwen James Kwen is a journalist with Leadership Media Group with 15 years of experience, currently covering politics, including the National Assembly (House of Representatives), APC, INEC, and allied beats",
