   "body": "The command’s spokesperson, DSP Orchia Peter Aondongu, confirmed the development to LEADERSHIP on Sunday evening in a telephone conversation, saying the rescued victims were taken to a hospital in Otukpo for medical attention. “Yes, our men this Sunday evening rescued the Catholic priest and seven other abducted victims. Two suspects were arrested. They were taken to a hospital in Otukpo for medical treatment,” Aondongu said. The rescue followed the abduction of Otache by unknown gunmen on Tuesday, October 13, 2026, along the Otobi Amejo-Ajegbe Road in Ohimini LGA. The Chancellor of the Catholic Diocese of Otukpo, Rev. Fr Joseph Aboyi Itodo, had earlier disclosed that the priest was ambushed and taken away by the gunmen while returning from Otukpo. The police said investigations into the incident were ongoing, while the rescued victims were receiving medical attention. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel BREAKING NEWS: Nigerians can invest ₦2.5million on premium domains and earn about ₦17-25Million. Earnings in USD. Rather than wonder, click here to find out how it works --> --> Aza Msue Aza Msue is a versatile journalist with 17 years of field experience. At LEADERSHIP Newspaper, he has published nonfiction articles that offer fresh perspectives on political, economic and social issues while highlighting positive impacts on society. His commitment to thoughtful reporting has contributed to public understanding and dialogue. He shares additional updates on X via @azamsue",
