   "_dt": 1792356822.0,
   "ageDays": 0.51,
   "summary": "Minister of the Federal Capital Territory, Chief Nyesom Wike and Rivers State Governor, Sir Siminalayi Fubara met in Port Harcourt in a strategic close door meeting ahead of the 2027 general election. Although details of the meeting, which was attended by supporters and loyalists of Fubara and Wike, were not made public, LEADERSHIP gathered that the gathering was part of efforts to strengthen the reconciliation within the Rainbow Coalition in the state.",
   "summary_zh": "联邦首都区部长Chief Nyesom Wike和河流州州长Sir Siminalayi Fubara在哈科特港举行了一次战略闭门会议，为2027年大选做准备。虽然这次由Fubara和Wike的支持者和忠实拥护者参加的会议细节并未公开，但LEADERSHIP gathered that the gathering was part of efforts to strengthen the reconciliation within the Rainbow Coalition in the state.",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Minister of the Federal Capital Territory, Chief Nyesom Wike and Rivers State Governor, Sir Siminalayi Fubara met in Port Harcourt in a strategic close door meeting ahead of the 2027 general election. Although details of the meeting, which was attended by supporters and loyalists of Fubara and Wike, were not made public, LEADERSHIP gathered that the gathering was part of efforts to strengthen the reconciliation within the Rainbow Coalition in the state. Among loyalists of the governor, who attended the meeting was his former Chief of Staff, Hon. Edison Ehie, who has been off the political radar for something now. Also in attendance were former representative of Rivers East Senatorial District, Senator George Sekibo and the Chairman, Rainbow Coalition Reconciliation Committee, Senator Magnus Abe. Others were the Speaker of the Rivers State House of Assembly, Rt. Hon. Martins Amaewhule and the All Progressives Congress (APC) governorship candidate in the state, Hon. Kingsly Chinda. Also in attendance were former Attorney General of Rivers State, Chief Adokiye Amiesimaka; former Chairman of the Peoples Democratic Party (PDP) in the state, Hon. Chukwuemeka Aaron and other stakeholders. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel BREAKING NEWS: Nigerians can invest ₦2.5million on premium domains and earn about ₦17-25Million. Earnings in USD. Rather than wonder, click here to find out how it works --> --> Anayo Onukwugha Anayo Onukwugha is a multiple award‑winning journalist with more than 20 years of experience. A former assistant secretary and acting secretary of the Rivers State Council of the Nigeria Union of Journalists, he now works with LEADERSHIP Newspaper. His articles address issues relating to the oil‑rich Niger Delta region, Nigeria and broader global topics. He shares his reporting journey on X at @aonukwugha",
