   "title": "Nigeria Leads Discussion On ECOWAS-AES Strategic Partnership",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/nigeria-leads-discussion-on-ecowas-aes-strategic-partnership",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:52:58 GMT",
   "_dt": 1792313578.0,
   "ageDays": 1.01,
   "summary": "Nigeria’s Minister of State for Foreign Affairs, Ambassador Sola Enikanolaiye, is leading the Nigerian Delegation in Dakar, Senegal for this strategic discussion, a statement issued on Friday by the Spokesman of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Oluwafemi Adeniyi said.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚外交部部长级官员、大使Sola Enikanolaiye正率领尼日利亚代表团在塞内加尔达喀尔参加此次战略讨论，外交部发言人Oluwafemi Adeniyi周五发表的声明说。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Nigeria’s Minister of State for Foreign Affairs, Ambassador Sola Enikanolaiye, is leading the Nigerian Delegation in Dakar, Senegal for this strategic discussion, a statement issued on Friday by the Spokesman of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Oluwafemi Adeniyi said. According to the statement, the primary objective of this first round of discussions is to prepare and align the strategic positions of ECOWAS member States and facilitate targeted and structured talks with the AES, at both the Ministerial and technical levels, to address shared regional issues comprehensively. “It is expected that at the end of this round of engagement, there would be concurrence on the draft General Framework Agreement between ECOWAS and AES Member States, ahead of the forthcoming end of the year Summit in Abuja in December 2026. “Nigeria, as a key founding member of ECOWAS, remains committed to the principles of regional integration, peace, and security. The presence of the Honourable Minister of State underscores Nigeria’s dedication to ensuring that the exit of the AES member states does not negatively impact on the age-long cultural and geographical ties between brother West African countries,” the statement added. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel BREAKING NEWS: Nigerians can invest ₦2.5million on premium domains and earn about ₦17-25Million. Earnings in USD. Rather than wonder, click here to find out how it works --> --> Innocent Odoh",
