   "_dt": 1792292400.0,
   "ageDays": 1.26,
   "summary": "PlamPay launched later, entering the Nigerian markets in 2019 after raising a $40 million seed round led by Chinese mobile phone maker Transsion. Between January and July 2020, mobile money transactions grew from N1.37 trillion to N41.54 trillion in the same period in 2024. Temitayo Jaiyeola October 6, 2024 5 min read Add BusinessDay as a preferred source on Google Follow BusinessDay on Google News Mobile money transactions rose by 2,472.75 per cent to 1.64 billion in 2023 from 63.79 million in 2020.",
   "summary_zh": "PlamPay 后来推出，在筹集由中国手机制造商 Transsion 领投的 4000 万美元种子轮后，于 2019 年进入尼日利亚市场。在 2020 年 1 月至 7 月期间，移动货币交易从 1.37 万亿奈拉增长到 2024 年同期的 41.54 万亿奈拉。Temitayo Jaiyeola 2024 年 10 月 6 日 5 分钟阅读 将 BusinessDay 添加为 Google 上的首选来源 在 Google 新闻上关注 BusinessDay 移动货币交易在 2023 年增长 2472.75% 至 16.4 亿笔，而 2020 年为 6379 万笔。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "PlamPay launched later, entering the Nigerian markets in 2019 after raising a $40 million seed round led by Chinese mobile phone maker Transsion. As part of the investment, PalmPay was preinstalled on Transsion’s mobile brands Tecno, Infinix, and Itel. Both fintechs achieved this by leveraging fundraising. OPay has raised $570 million so far, while PalmPay has raised $400 million. “Their success can be attributed to first their financial strength. Top players must have deep resources,” noted Olojo. Chinese fintechs rule as Nigeria’s mobile money value jumps 29-fold Between January and July 2020, mobile money transactions grew from N1.37 trillion to N41.54 trillion in the same period in 2024. Temitayo Jaiyeola October 6, 2024 5 min read Add BusinessDay as a preferred source on Google Follow BusinessDay on Google News Mobile money transactions rose by 2,472.75 per cent to 1.64 billion in 2023 from 63.79 million in 2020. Despite boasting 17 companies licensed by the CBN as mobile money operators (non-bank-led), this growth has been driven by Chinese fintech companies Opay and Palmpay",
