   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "The President also directed the new ambassador to Israel, Evelyn Korantemaa Ofosu-Amable, to uphold Ghana’s position on Palestine. “We recognise the sovereign State of Palestine and support a viable two-state solution in which Israel and Palestine will live side by side in peace and security within internationally recognised and secure borders,” he said. He added that Ghana’s international engagements must uphold international law, protect civilians and respect human dignity. President Mahama urged all four envoys to work closely with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, follow government policy and use public resources responsibly. He reminded them that Article 40 of the 1992 Constitution should guide their conduct in promoting and protecting Ghana’s interests abroad",
