   "summary": "The Minister of Lands and Natural Resources, Emmanuel Armah-Kofi Buah, has reaffirmed Ghana’s readiness to partner with Guangdong Shengmai Tech Co. Ltd. to explore investment opportunities in the country’s mineral sector. Speaking during a meeting with a delegation from the Chinese company, the Minister said Ghana was interested in investors who looked beyond short-term profits and were committed to developing the communities in which they operated.",
   "summary_zh": "土地和自然资源部长埃马纽埃尔·阿尔马-科菲·布阿重申，加纳已准备好与广东生脉科技有限公司合作，探索该国矿业领域的投资机会。在与中国公司代表团会晤时，部长表示，加纳对那些超越短期利润、致力于发展其运营所在社区的投资者感兴趣。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "The Minister of Lands and Natural Resources, Emmanuel Armah-Kofi Buah, has reaffirmed Ghana’s readiness to partner with Guangdong Shengmai Tech Co. Ltd. to explore investment opportunities in the country’s mineral sector. Speaking during a meeting with a delegation from the Chinese company, the Minister said Ghana was interested in investors who looked beyond short-term profits and were committed to developing the communities in which they operated. Buah also underscored the importance of responsible mining practices, noting that investors must prioritise environmental protection and the restoration of mined-out areas. Tang highlighted the use of modern electromagnetic technology for mineral exploration, which he said could significantly reduce the time and resources required for exploration while promoting environmental sustainability and value addition. He said the company was willing to work with the Ministry and other relevant agencies to identify opportunities where its expertise could support the development of Ghana’s mineral sector. Armah-Kofi Buah with a delegation from Guangdong Shengmai Tech Co. Ltd Armah-Kofi Buah with a delegation from Guangdong Shengmai Tech Co. Ltd",
