   "title": "Tinubu orders security chiefs to rescue abductees clear bandit camps",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/tinubu-orders-security-chiefs-to-rescue-abductees-clear-bandit-camps",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:12:44 GMT",
   "_dt": 1792095164.0,
   "ageDays": 3.54,
   "summary": "Musa, who spoke to State House correspondents on Thursday after a security meeting presided over by the President at the Presidential Villa, Abuja, said Tinubu also asked the service chiefs and other security heads to guarantee a safe environment for Nigerians to vote in the elections scheduled for January. The minister said the meeting was convened to brief the President on the security situation ahead of the polls, with all heads of security agencies in attendance.",
   "summary_zh": "穆萨周四在阿布贾总统别墅由总统主持的安全会议后对国家宫记者发表讲话时表示，蒂努布还要求各军种参谋长和其他安全负责人确保为尼日利亚人参加定于1月举行的选举提供安全环境。部长说，召开这次会议是为了向总统通报选举前的安全局势，所有安全机构负责人均出席了会议。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Musa, who spoke to State House correspondents on Thursday after a security meeting presided over by the President at the Presidential Villa, Abuja, said Tinubu also asked the service chiefs and other security heads to guarantee a safe environment for Nigerians to vote in the elections scheduled for January. The minister said the meeting was convened to brief the President on the security situation ahead of the polls, with all heads of security agencies in attendance. “The directive from the President is: all of us must go all out to fish out and rescue all those that have been abducted, kidnapped, wherever they are. Tinubu orders security chiefs to rescue abductees, clear bandit camps The minister urged Nigerians to support the security agencies, including by reporting wrongdoing by security personnel. He argued, “Security is everybody’s responsibility. It’s not only for members of security forces. Everyone has a role to play. “Whatever you see that is going wrong, even with our members that are not doing what is right, please don’t hesitate to report. Action will be taken.” The meeting was attended by the National Security Adviser, Nuhu Ribadu; the Minister of Police Affairs, Ibrahim Gaidam; the Minister of State for Defence, Bello Matawalle; and the Special Adviser to the President on Homeland Security, Maj. Gen. Adeyinka Famadewa (retd.)",
   "bodyLevel": "excerpt",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "四国政府",
