   "summary": "Energy and Green Transition Minister Dr John Jinapor says the government has secured $3.5 billion in investment commitments to expand operations and drill new wells as part of efforts to revitalise Ghana’s upstream petroleum sector and restore investor confidence. He emphasised that attracting investment alone was not enough. According to the Minister, the approach was already yielding encouraging results, with significant investment commitments and positive developments in crude oil production.",
   "summary_zh": "能源和绿色转型部长Dr John Jinapor表示，政府已获得35亿美元的投资承诺，以扩大运营和钻探新井，作为振兴加纳上游石油部门和恢复投资者信心的努力的一部分。他强调，仅吸引投资是不够的。根据部长所说，这种方法已经产生了令人鼓舞的结果，带来了大量投资承诺和原油生产的积极发展。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Energy and Green Transition Minister Dr John Jinapor says the government has secured $3.5 billion in investment commitments to expand operations and drill new wells as part of efforts to revitalise Ghana’s upstream petroleum sector and restore investor confidence. He emphasised that attracting investment alone was not enough. Ghana must also ensure that its petroleum resources deliver lasting economic benefits for its people. He stressed that the reforms were intended to attract fresh capital while safeguarding Ghana’s national interests. According to the Minister, the approach was already yielding encouraging results, with significant investment commitments and positive developments in crude oil production. He said the government’s next priority was to sustain the momentum, increase local participation and deepen domestic value addition across the petroleum value chain",
