   "snippet": "The Nigeria-US Critical Minerals Framework (signed 23 Sept 2026) is a non-binding policy plan for cooperation on mining, processing, investment, geological mapping, recycling and supply-chain security for critical minerals and rare earths. No legal obligations or fixed funding.\n\nFor Nigeria: attracts US capital and expertise for local processing, jobs, skills and value addition beyond raw exports; aids resource mapping.\n\nFor USA: diversifies secure supplies for tech, defence and industry; first-look investment options in Nigerian assets; reduces reliance on other sources.\n\nThe $700bn figure is Nigeria’s preliminary mineral-wealth estimate, not committed money.",
