   "url": "https://x.com/nigerianports/status/2111092639990775914",
   "snippet": "The Managing Director, Dr. @AbuDantsoho, today joined the Honourable Minister of Marine and Blue Economy, Dr. Adegboyega Oyetola, heads of sister agencies, and industry experts to commemorate World Maritime Day.\n\nSpeaking on this year’s theme, “From Policy to Practice: Powering Maritime Excellence,” the Managing Director noted that while sea transport is among the most environmentally friendly modes, the real test lies in the continuous implementation of protective policies. He highlighted how the Nigerian Ports Authority, under his stewardship, has moved from policy to practice by consistently promoting port eco-friendliness.\n\nHe further emphasised the critical role of Nigerian ports in national trade, noting that a greater percentage of export transactions contributing to Nigeria’s ₦12 trillion trade surplus in the second quarter of 2026 passed through the country’s ports.\n\nAs part of the celebration, the Nigerian Ports Authority also presented awards to secondary school students who participated in a quiz competition.\n\n#WorldMaritimeDay2026",
